ja:
量子力学的な波に対して、運動量は $p=\frac{h}{\lambda}
=\frac{2\pi\hbar}{\lambda}
=\hbar k.$ である。したがって、$k$と$p$は因子$\hbar$だけ異なる。正と負の$k$は、反対方向に進む波と、反対向きの運動量をもつ粒子を表す。$\hbar=1$とする単位系では、$k$をそれ以上区別せずに運動量と呼ぶのが通例である。

zh:
对于量子力学波，动量为 $p=\frac{h}{\lambda}
=\frac{2\pi\hbar}{\lambda}
=\hbar k.$ 因此$k$与$p$只相差因子$\hbar$。正的和负的$k$描述沿相反方向运动的波以及动量方向相反的粒子。在$\hbar=1$的单位制下，通常就把$k$称为动量，不再作进一步区分。

p.src:
The annihilation field acts first: $\begin{aligned}\Psi(x)|k_{\mathrm{initial}}\rangle
&=\sum_q e^{iqx}a(q)a^\dagger(k_{\mathrm{initial}})|0\rangle.\end{aligned}$ Every term vanishes except the one with $q=k_{\mathrm{initial}}$. An annihilation operator has to find a particle in its own mode. Hence $\Psi(x)|k_{\mathrm{initial}}\rangle
=e^{ik_{\mathrm{initial}}x}|0\rangle.$ The two creation fields then give $\begin{aligned}&\Psi^\dagger(x)\Psi^\dagger(x)\Psi(x)
|k_{\mathrm{initial}}\rangle
\\
&\quad=
e^{ik_{\mathrm{initial}}x}
\sum_{\ell,m}
e^{-i\ell x}e^{-imx}
a^\dagger(\ell)a^\dagger(m)|0\rangle
\\
&\quad=
\sum_{\ell,m}
e^{i(k_{\mathrm{initial}}-\ell-m)x}
a^\dagger(\ell)a^\dagger(m)|0\rangle.\end{aligned}$ For unequal $\ell$ and $m$, the operator state may be denoted $|\ell,m\rangle$: one particle occupies each of the two modes. The final result is a sum over all such two-particle momentum configurations, with a phase determined by the incoming and outgoing momenta.

